      "content": "It sounds like your partner might be experiencing symptoms of hypoglycemia (low blood sugar), which can cause confusion, sleepiness, and nausea. Drinking water can help, but it's crucial they check their blood sugar levels to confirm. If they don't have a glucose meter or can't afford one, encourage them to eat a quick, sugary snack and monitor their symptoms closely. If they can't feel better soon or if blood sugar levels are very low, seek emergency medical help immediately. Stay calm and supportive.",
